 "fnTech3": {
  "before": "s_language registered only for Elite Force; jk2-mp got it from ui.qvm's cvar table, jk2-sp never; no Outcast load read it",
  "change": [
   "code/client/audio/snd_main.cpp S_Init: Com_GameIsJK2() registers s_language \"english\", CVAR_ARCHIVE | CVAR_NORESTART, before the s_initsound check",
   "code/client/audio/codecs/snd_codec.cpp: S_JK2ForeignVoice (first \"chars\" -> chr_d/chr_f by s_language; case-sensitive in jk2-mp, any case in jk2-sp) and S_CodecLoad: the foreign <name>.wav quietly first (.wav, .mp3, .ogg), then the English one"
  ],
  "differencesRecorded": [
   "the OpenAL backend lowercases every registered name (NormalizeSoundName) before loading, so there a multiplayer \"Chars\" finds the foreign recording; the legacy mixer keeps case and matches retail; no installed name has such a \"chars\"",
   "com_buildScript foreign-file opening and its multiplayer .mp3 slip are not reproduced",
   "Fn tries Ogg Vorbis after .mp3 for the foreign name too; no Outcast voice is Ogg Vorbis",
   "developer note \"Sound fallback: ...chr_d/x.wav -> ...chr_d/x.mp3\" names each foreign voice; a missing foreign recording prints nothing, as retail",
   "jk2-sp cinematic voice track and German g_dismemberment rule not served (no jk2-sp client)"
  ]
 },
